WEBVTT

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:24.942
As the curtain rises
on our verisimilitudinous tableau,

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:28.111
you're no doubt curious
as to why I tricked you all

00:00:28.195 --> 00:00:30.113
into hang gliding here.

00:00:30.197 --> 00:00:31.240
Close-up.

00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:35.160
It seems someone in this room
is a murderer.

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:40.249
It's me.
But the real question is,

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:42.376
which of you is the victim?

00:00:42.626 --> 00:00:47.214
And that secret I shall take to my grave.

00:00:47.506 --> 00:00:48.674
Calculon, no!

00:00:55.973 --> 00:00:57.307
Now, that's acting.

00:00:57.558 --> 00:01:00.894
Calculon really Shatnered
the hell out of that scene.

00:01:00.978 --> 00:01:03.272
Hey, anyone want to go to the aquarium?

00:01:03.397 --> 00:01:05.691
They got a new non-biting otter.

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:07.526
- Sounds great!
- Non-biting otter!

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:17.953
Wow. Aquariums have really
changed since I was a boy

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:19.454
and no one ever took me to them.

00:01:19.538 --> 00:01:20.622
Where's the glass?

00:01:20.706 --> 00:01:23.333
There isn't any. The water's
held in place by gravity fields

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:25.752
so there's nothing
for kids to smear yogurt on.

00:01:25.836 --> 00:01:28.505
I like strawberry yogurt.
Can I touch the water?

00:01:28.589 --> 00:01:30.465
I wouldn't, but I'm smart.

00:01:31.425 --> 00:01:32.467
Ahhh!

00:01:32.551 --> 00:01:33.760
Help. Police.

00:01:33.844 --> 00:01:35.053
Neat.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:41.435
Welcome to Jurassic Tank.

00:01:47.024 --> 00:01:48.901
Picture time.
Everybody get together.

00:01:51.695 --> 00:01:56.116
Hang on, I need a tripod.
Let me just extend the old third leg.

00:01:57.451 --> 00:02:00.829
Ooh, yeah. That's stable, baby.
Just need to pick a lens.

00:02:00.913 --> 00:02:03.290
Let's see, zoom lens?

00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:04.875
Nope.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.043
They Live lens?

00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:08.629
Eh... So-so.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.923
Twilight Zone
one-minute-in-the-future lens?

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.010
Ooh, Calculon's going to be here.
Better get my camera ready.

00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:16.553
Just take the damn picture.

00:02:17.054 --> 00:02:21.141
Let me just adjust the focus,
F-stop, shutter speed.

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:23.685
Oops! Out of film. Hang on.

00:02:23.769 --> 00:02:25.395
Seriously.

00:02:25.479 --> 00:02:27.064
Film? Who uses film?

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.191
We've had digital cameras
for a thousand years.

00:02:29.441 --> 00:02:30.859
Digital?

00:02:30.943 --> 00:02:34.571
No digital camera can capture
the warmth and grain of good old film.

00:02:34.905 --> 00:02:38.242
How can you even tell?
Your eyes are digital cameras.

00:02:38.325 --> 00:02:41.411
And where can you possibly
get film developed nowadays?

00:02:41.578 --> 00:02:42.955
Right here.

00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:46.542
You're looking at
the last chemical darkroom in existence.

00:02:46.625 --> 00:02:48.335
Hey, Bender,
isn't that Calculon?

00:02:48.418 --> 00:02:50.587
Calculon? No way!

00:02:50.671 --> 00:02:52.422
Oh! Oh! Oh!

00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:56.301
Yo, Calky!
I'm a big fan, and I've got a big camera.

00:02:56.385 --> 00:02:57.511
Can I get a big picture?

00:02:58.762 --> 00:03:02.015
Well, I was just airbrushed this morning,
so all right.

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:03.267
But make it snappy.

00:03:04.977 --> 00:03:06.019
That looked staged.

00:03:06.103 --> 00:03:08.230
Try one where you're pretending
to swing a tennis racquet.

00:03:10.524 --> 00:03:12.484
Okay, okay, that's enough.

00:03:12.568 --> 00:03:14.611
I'm trying to enjoy a nice day out

00:03:14.736 --> 00:03:16.822
with the actors who play my TV family.

00:03:18.866 --> 00:03:21.159
These rare and fascinating deep-sea fish

00:03:21.285 --> 00:03:23.620
are extremely sensitive to light.

00:03:23.871 --> 00:03:27.291
Over here, Calculon!
Come on, smile. Quit blinking. Red eye.

00:03:27.374 --> 00:03:28.667
Blurry. Lens cap's still on.

00:03:32.546 --> 00:03:36.091
Oh! We finally eluded
that obnoxious shutterbug.

00:03:36.175 --> 00:03:40.179
At last, we can enjoy
our studio-mandated quality time.

00:03:42.097 --> 00:03:44.933
Argh! I can't not work like this.

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:47.311
I'll be in my day-off trailer.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:57.654
And I took this one inside
the ichthyosaur's stomach.

00:03:57.738 --> 00:04:01.825
Man, I've never had
anyone try so hard to digest me.

00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:04.745
Look, we've all been
in a sea monster's stomach.

00:04:04.828 --> 00:04:07.080
But did you get any pictures
of the Calculon?

00:04:07.206 --> 00:04:11.084
Yeah, but a true photo buff
wouldn't even use these for toilet paper.

00:04:11.168 --> 00:04:12.836
Not if curtains were available.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.671
You're too hard on yourself, robot.

00:04:14.838 --> 00:04:16.507
These pictures are just as good

00:04:16.715 --> 00:04:18.342
as the ones in my celebrity tabloid.

00:04:18.592 --> 00:04:20.135
Us People Magazine?

00:04:20.219 --> 00:04:21.470
That's total trash.

00:04:21.553 --> 00:04:23.180
Total celebrity trash.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.516
My inquiring organ wants to know.

00:04:25.599 --> 00:04:26.642
If you ask me,

00:04:26.725 --> 00:04:29.311
Bender should go
to Us People's office in Hollywood

00:04:29.394 --> 00:04:30.854
and see if they'd like
his Calculon pictures.

00:04:32.523 --> 00:04:34.942
I have no time for such foolishness.

00:04:37.819 --> 00:04:40.447
Well, I changed my mind and
came to Hollywood after all.

00:04:40.864 --> 00:04:43.116
Bender, these shots of Calculon are great.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.745
In fact, you might
just have what it takes to be a paparazzo.

00:04:46.828 --> 00:04:47.871
Namely, a camera.

00:04:48.038 --> 00:04:49.289
Shut up. I know it.

00:04:49.373 --> 00:04:50.958
Wait, a what's-a-whatzo?

00:04:51.041 --> 00:04:54.378
A paparazzo.
You know, a celebrity photographer.

00:04:54.461 --> 00:04:55.754
But it's not for everyone.

00:04:55.838 --> 00:04:57.714
You'd have to wallow in Hollywood filth,

00:04:57.798 --> 00:05:00.634
loiter in dark alleys
behind seedy nightclubs

00:05:00.717 --> 00:05:03.095
and get spat on by the beautiful people.

00:05:03.387 --> 00:05:05.639
Hmm, I don't know.
How much will it cost me?

00:05:05.722 --> 00:05:08.559
You misunderstand, Bender.
We'll pay you.

00:05:11.103 --> 00:05:14.898
Sir, you just hired yourself
a new what's-a-whatzo.

00:05:20.863 --> 00:05:23.490
Listen up, gang,
I'd like to introduce you to Bender,

00:05:23.574 --> 00:05:26.118
the newest member
of our paparazzo family.

00:05:26.201 --> 00:05:28.996
Nice to meet you.
And even though it's only my first day,

00:05:30.122 --> 00:05:31.832
I want you all to know
that I'm already better than you.

00:05:31.915 --> 00:05:33.000
Stay out of my way!

00:06:10.037 --> 00:06:12.164
I'm back, Crab Dip.
What you watching?

00:06:12.414 --> 00:06:15.751
Only a documentary
about the greatest actor in the world.

00:06:16.084 --> 00:06:17.794
Ah, yes, Calculon.

00:06:17.878 --> 00:06:19.630
I happened to snap a picture of him

00:06:19.796 --> 00:06:21.590
taking some time with his biggest fan.

00:06:21.673 --> 00:06:24.092
No, not that scene-chewing ham.

00:06:24.176 --> 00:06:28.972
I said the greatest actor,
Langdon Cobb. Let's rewind, shall we?

00:06:31.308 --> 00:06:35.229
Langdon Cobb, the most
acclaimed actor of his generation.

00:06:35.312 --> 00:06:36.939
Why's he wearing a bag on his head?

00:06:37.022 --> 00:06:39.149
They're explaining that right now.

00:06:39.233 --> 00:06:41.109
Let's rewind again.

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.947
...most acclaimed
actor of his generation.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:48.200
He's raked in seven Academy Awards
for best actor

00:06:48.283 --> 00:06:49.826
and two for best actress,

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:53.247
all without ever removing
his trademark bag.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.917
Mr. Cobb, you're an intensely private man.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.043
Quite right.
Mmm-hmm.

00:06:58.126 --> 00:07:00.295
And though billions of people
have seen your work...

00:07:00.379 --> 00:07:03.006
- Mmm-hmm.
- ...no one has ever seen your face.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:05.509
So tell us, why the bag?

00:07:05.592 --> 00:07:09.930
Ah, yes, the bag. I've never understood
people's fascination with that.

00:07:10.013 --> 00:07:13.225
The point is, I'm an actor
and nothing more.

00:07:13.308 --> 00:07:14.810
I have no interest in being admired

00:07:14.893 --> 00:07:16.979
for something as inconsequential

00:07:17.104 --> 00:07:19.147
as my appearance or my personal life.

00:07:19.231 --> 00:07:22.568
All that truly matters is the process.

00:07:23.068 --> 00:07:25.737
Whether playing
a beloved historical figure.

00:07:25.821 --> 00:07:29.157
For Rigel 7 and all mankind!

00:07:29.324 --> 00:07:31.743
Or a Victorian circus freak...

00:07:32.035 --> 00:07:34.580
I want to see the real you.

00:07:34.663 --> 00:07:35.873
No, Daisy, don't!

00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:40.460
I tried to warn you.
I'm hideous.

00:07:40.544 --> 00:07:43.630
To me, you're beautiful.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:48.468
...Langdon Cobb's
acting is always in the bag.

00:07:48.552 --> 00:07:51.763
Truly, his is the most
famous face in Hollywood.

00:07:51.847 --> 00:07:56.560
Even if no one's ever photographed it,
nor ever will.

00:07:56.768 --> 00:08:00.522
Once again,
television has given me a reason to live.

00:08:01.106 --> 00:08:04.943
A photo of Langdon Cobb
without his bag? Impossible.

00:08:05.027 --> 00:08:07.863
He's got a 50-foot-high force field
around his house.

00:08:08.572 --> 00:08:10.657
One 60-foot ladder, please.

00:08:27.216 --> 00:08:28.258
Oh!

00:08:28.342 --> 00:08:30.302
What are you, some kind of attack fungus?

00:08:30.385 --> 00:08:31.929
Or just a moldy schnauzer?

00:08:33.931 --> 00:08:36.183
Oh, God,
please let this tacky Hollywood mansion

00:08:36.266 --> 00:08:39.561
have the obligatory...
Yes! Tuscan-inspired pergola!

00:08:42.731 --> 00:08:44.775
Peace out, Portobello.

00:08:48.362 --> 00:08:49.404
Thank you, Leroy.

00:08:49.488 --> 00:08:51.740
I'm going to relax by the fire
with my bag off,

00:08:51.823 --> 00:08:53.367
so that will be all for the night.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:54.952
By your command.

00:08:58.247 --> 00:09:00.499
Come to paparazzo.

00:09:08.757 --> 00:09:10.050
- Gotcha!
- No!

00:09:11.134 --> 00:09:14.638
Please, sir, I implore you,
destroy that photo of me.

00:09:14.721 --> 00:09:17.599
It's not just my privacy
I've been protecting all these years.

00:09:17.683 --> 00:09:19.476
If you show anyone that picture,

00:09:19.601 --> 00:09:21.353
there will be terrible consequences.

00:09:21.478 --> 00:09:24.273
The only thing terrible is
going to be my bank account.

00:09:24.356 --> 00:09:27.693
Wait. Say that again, but say,
"Tremendous consequences."

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:30.571
If it's money you're after,
I'll pay whatever you ask.

00:09:30.654 --> 00:09:34.157
Just promise me
you'll never show that photo to anyone.

00:09:34.491 --> 00:09:37.786
I swear on my honor as a paparazzo.

00:09:38.495 --> 00:09:39.663
Hey, Fry, want to see a picture?

00:09:39.788 --> 00:09:40.914
Sure.

00:09:45.752 --> 00:09:48.463
Hmm... He looked at the photo
and that happened.

00:09:48.547 --> 00:09:50.716
But it could just be a coincidence.

00:09:50.966 --> 00:09:52.134
Yo, Amy, check it out.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:57.723
The evidence is mounting.

00:09:57.806 --> 00:10:00.017
Although two times
hardly establishes a pattern.

00:10:00.309 --> 00:10:01.894
I'd feel more comfortable
raising the alarm

00:10:01.977 --> 00:10:03.478
if I were a little more certain.

00:10:03.562 --> 00:10:05.272
Hey, how'd those two get deflated?

00:10:05.355 --> 00:10:06.481
They looked at this.

00:10:10.319 --> 00:10:11.403
That proves it.

00:10:11.486 --> 00:10:13.614
Looking at this photo of Langdon Cobb

00:10:13.697 --> 00:10:15.908
has a horrific effect on living creatures.

00:10:16.491 --> 00:10:19.119
Hey, Zoidberg,
look at this photo of Langdon Cobb.

00:10:19.203 --> 00:10:21.330
What, a picture of Langdon Cobb?

00:10:21.413 --> 00:10:24.291
Now, this I want to see
as clearly as possible.

00:10:24.374 --> 00:10:26.376
Zoidberg, no!

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:32.591
Oh, thank God, Professor.
You got here just in time.

00:10:33.258 --> 00:10:34.760
I've seen this before.

00:10:34.927 --> 00:10:37.721
Langdon Cobb must be from Bryoria Six,

00:10:37.888 --> 00:10:40.349
home of the quantum lichen people.

00:10:40.432 --> 00:10:42.184
Well, that explains that.

00:10:42.309 --> 00:10:46.980
They're attention parasites.
They feed on the admiration of their prey.

00:10:47.064 --> 00:10:48.649
Just like the noble buffalo.

00:10:48.732 --> 00:10:50.192
Nothing like a buffalo.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:54.029
Anyone who pays attention to the lichen
is unknowingly feeding it.

00:10:54.112 --> 00:10:57.407
But gaze upon its face,
even in a photograph,

00:10:57.491 --> 00:11:02.371
and your very life force will be
sucked out, leaving you a flaccid husk.

00:11:02.538 --> 00:11:04.665
So the picture robbed them of their souls?

00:11:04.831 --> 00:11:09.378
Souls? Don't be ridiculous. It's their
life forces that have been stolen.

00:11:09.461 --> 00:11:10.671
It's scientific.

00:11:10.754 --> 00:11:13.882
That's why the robot's immune.
He has no soul.

00:11:13.966 --> 00:11:15.175
Life force!

00:11:15.259 --> 00:11:18.262
So, how do we get their life forces back?

00:11:18.345 --> 00:11:19.888
If we poke a hole in Cobb's bag,

00:11:19.972 --> 00:11:23.308
will they spew out like a volcano
built on an Indian graveyard?

00:11:23.392 --> 00:11:25.519
Alas, it's not that simple.

00:11:25.602 --> 00:11:27.604
You see, just as the Earth lichen

00:11:27.729 --> 00:11:29.731
is composed of an algae and a fungus,

00:11:29.815 --> 00:11:34.361
the quantum variety
is also composed of two separate parts.

00:11:34.444 --> 00:11:39.783
An attractive algae-based id
and a ravenous fungus-based ego

00:11:39.867 --> 00:11:44.121
that stores the stolen souls.
I mean, life forces.

00:11:44.788 --> 00:11:46.790
Now, here's the weird part.

00:11:46.874 --> 00:11:48.667
The ego and the id are connected

00:11:48.834 --> 00:11:52.462
not physically,
like decent, God-fearing Earth lichens,

00:11:52.546 --> 00:11:54.840
but by quantum entanglement.

00:11:56.133 --> 00:11:59.386
So the id is Langdon Cobb,
but this fungus ego could be...

00:11:59.469 --> 00:12:01.513
Anywhere!
We'll never find it.

00:12:01.597 --> 00:12:04.308
Let's just give up and
go to the aquarium again.

00:12:04.391 --> 00:12:08.103
Now, hold on. I feel like
I was chased by a mushroom recently.

00:12:08.187 --> 00:12:10.939
Of course!
The guard dog at Cobb's estate.

00:12:11.023 --> 00:12:12.065
That's the ego.

00:12:12.149 --> 00:12:14.860
All right, let's go.
It'll be just like stomping a puppy.

00:12:14.943 --> 00:12:19.156
No, no, no.
Subduing an actor's ego is no easy task.

00:12:19.281 --> 00:12:20.949
We'll have to weaken it first.

00:12:21.033 --> 00:12:23.744
Look, I own words that are helpful.

00:12:23.827 --> 00:12:26.997
It says the World Acting Championship
is tonight in Hollywood.

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:29.666
Quiet, Zoidberg.
God, I wish you were a husk.

00:12:29.791 --> 00:12:32.836
No, it's Langdon Cobb versus Calculon.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:36.507
If we help Calculon win,
it will weaken Cobb's ego, maybe?

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:38.592
Yes, yes, fine.

00:12:38.842 --> 00:12:41.470
We never go
where I want to go.

00:12:41.845 --> 00:12:46.475
So, the most galling of the paparazzi
needs my help.

00:12:46.558 --> 00:12:48.977
Lo, the worm has turned.

00:12:49.061 --> 00:12:51.647
Say cheese, Calculon without makeup.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:56.235
As much as I hate you,
I hate Langdon Cobb more.

00:12:56.401 --> 00:12:58.403
He beats me out for every award,

00:12:58.529 --> 00:13:00.531
every role, every paternity suit.

00:13:00.739 --> 00:13:04.993
Besting him at acting
means more to me than life itself.

00:13:05.118 --> 00:13:06.203
And we want to help you.

00:13:06.286 --> 00:13:08.705
Now, your only chance
is a classic death scene.

00:13:08.789 --> 00:13:10.999
One with a lot of "thy's" and "thou's."

00:13:11.083 --> 00:13:14.586
Voilà. The tragic end of
Rome O. and Julie T.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:18.507
That's Romeo and Juliet,
dummy, by Will.i.am Shakespeare.

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:21.635
Now, here's the poison
that Romeo uses to kill himself.

00:13:21.718 --> 00:13:23.929
Don't worry, it's just water
and food coloring.

00:13:24.012 --> 00:13:25.097
Food coloring?

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:28.225
The most poisonous substance
known to robots?

00:13:28.308 --> 00:13:31.311
Oops! Sorry. I'll swap it out
for harmless battery acid.

00:13:31.395 --> 00:13:33.063
No. Wait.

00:13:33.397 --> 00:13:35.941
There's only one way to ensure victory.

00:13:36.066 --> 00:13:39.361
I must perform the ultimate death scene.

00:13:39.611 --> 00:13:44.533
I shall drink the actual poison
and actually die.

00:13:45.367 --> 00:13:47.828
But, Calculon, you can't kill yourself.

00:13:48.036 --> 00:13:50.539
I'm a celebrity.
I can kill anyone I want.

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:01.216
Call it in the air.

00:14:01.383 --> 00:14:02.593
Comedy.

00:14:03.218 --> 00:14:06.722
It's tragedy. Langdon Cobb
will be first to take the stage.

00:14:07.431 --> 00:14:09.266
Bossy to Stinky.
Come in, Stinky.

00:14:09.349 --> 00:14:10.809
I always come in stinky.

00:14:11.101 --> 00:14:13.270
Stand by.
The competition's about to begin.

00:14:13.353 --> 00:14:14.438
Oh!

00:14:14.521 --> 00:14:17.774
Hold your fire until Calculon's
performanceweakens the ego.

00:14:17.941 --> 00:14:19.526
Roger. Stinky over.

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:21.737
Whoof! I beg to differ.

00:14:23.197 --> 00:14:24.865
I wish it had been me, Sully.

00:14:24.948 --> 00:14:26.867
I wish it had been me off-duty
in the Garden

00:14:27.868 --> 00:14:29.745
when those drug lords blew up the Celtics.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:32.581
But I was drunk, wicked drunk.

00:14:32.664 --> 00:14:35.792
Uh-oh. Cobb's doing a scene
from Beantown Buddies.

00:14:35.876 --> 00:14:38.962
The audience is eating it up.
Professor, what's your status?

00:14:39.046 --> 00:14:40.130
Not good.

00:14:40.797 --> 00:14:43.884
The attention Cobb's receiving
is inflating his ego.

00:14:44.051 --> 00:14:47.513
It's going totally Kanye.

00:14:47.596 --> 00:14:48.680
Wow!

00:14:48.764 --> 00:14:50.974
There's a humungous fungus among us.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:55.604
Oh, Sully,
you were the best partner I ever had,

00:14:55.687 --> 00:14:57.189
both on the beat

00:14:57.272 --> 00:14:59.149
and in the sack.

00:14:59.233 --> 00:15:01.860
That's right, I said it.

00:15:02.611 --> 00:15:03.779
I said it.

00:15:17.876 --> 00:15:19.670
A tough act to follow.

00:15:19.753 --> 00:15:22.047
And now, to follow that act,

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:25.342
performing the death scene
from Romeo and Juliet,

00:15:25.425 --> 00:15:29.805
seven-time Oscar runner-up, Calculon!

00:15:40.315 --> 00:15:42.359
Ah, dear Juliet,

00:15:42.693 --> 00:15:45.153
why art thou yet so fair?

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:47.155
I will stay with thee

00:15:47.239 --> 00:15:51.618
and never from this
palace of dim night depart again.

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:55.747
Oh, here will I set up my everlasting rest

00:15:55.831 --> 00:16:01.628
and shake the yoke of inauspicious stars
from this world-wearied flesh.

00:16:02.379 --> 00:16:05.215
Eyes, look your last.

00:16:05.299 --> 00:16:08.719
Arms, take your last embrace.

00:16:08.802 --> 00:16:15.726
And lips, oh, you, the doors of breath,
seal with a righteous kiss.

00:16:19.688 --> 00:16:21.273
Here's to my love.

00:16:34.036 --> 00:16:35.954
I can't believe he really did it.

00:16:36.038 --> 00:16:39.499
At least he died
knowing I was great.

00:16:48.967 --> 00:16:50.010
Uh-oh.

00:16:50.093 --> 00:16:52.346
That death scene
was almost half believable.

00:16:52.596 --> 00:16:55.140
Cobb looks jealous and insecure.
How's his ego doing?

00:16:55.474 --> 00:16:58.352
It's shrinking.
Faster, Professor, kill, kill.

00:16:58.477 --> 00:17:01.146
Activating anti-fungal ray.

00:17:02.981 --> 00:17:06.068
It just has to warm up
for about 15 minutes.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:11.907
Ladies and gentlemen and smizmars,

00:17:12.115 --> 00:17:14.451
we have a unanimous decision.

00:17:14.535 --> 00:17:18.455
The winner and
Heavyweight Acting Champion of the world,

00:17:18.539 --> 00:17:21.542
Langdon Cobb!

00:17:28.423 --> 00:17:29.466
Huh.

00:17:29.758 --> 00:17:32.636
Thank you. Thank you. Thanks.

00:17:32.719 --> 00:17:35.222
Oh, God, he's basking in their admiration.

00:17:35.305 --> 00:17:38.225
That ego must be at
least four feet tall by now.

00:17:50.904 --> 00:17:52.614
Aw! Did you miss me, pookie?

00:17:53.031 --> 00:17:54.575
- Ow!
- Oh!

00:17:54.658 --> 00:17:57.244
I can't watch.
I better take some pictures.

00:17:57.619 --> 00:17:58.704
Wait a minute.

00:17:58.787 --> 00:18:00.706
When living creatures look
at Cobb's photo,

00:18:00.789 --> 00:18:02.749
their life force gets sucked out.

00:18:02.833 --> 00:18:04.543
And Cobb's a living creature.

00:18:04.626 --> 00:18:06.837
I just need to show him
a picture of himself.

00:18:07.004 --> 00:18:09.423
But I tore up the only picture of Cobb.

00:18:09.506 --> 00:18:10.591
And everybody knows,

00:18:10.674 --> 00:18:13.218
once you delete a photo,
it's gone forever.

00:18:13.427 --> 00:18:14.970
Maybe a digital photo,

00:18:15.053 --> 00:18:17.556
but with film, I still have the negative.

00:18:17.639 --> 00:18:19.141
Hurry, make a new print.

00:18:19.224 --> 00:18:21.393
I don't know
how long I can distract Cobb's ego.

00:18:21.476 --> 00:18:23.228
Okay. I'll be in the darkroom.

00:18:31.737 --> 00:18:34.406
Eh...
Contrast is a little off on this one.

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:39.912
Oh!

00:18:39.995 --> 00:18:41.330
Bender, hurry up!

00:18:42.623 --> 00:18:44.249
This one is really good.

00:18:44.333 --> 00:18:46.335
But I can still do better.

00:18:48.045 --> 00:18:50.506
Who are you people?
Why are you attacking my ego?

00:18:50.589 --> 00:18:52.633
You stole our friends' life forces.

00:18:52.841 --> 00:18:56.595
Ah, yes. I warned the robot,
but he wouldn't listen.

00:18:56.678 --> 00:18:59.848
You see, I was once
like the rest of my species,

00:18:59.932 --> 00:19:03.685
showing my face to one planet,
draining its life force and moving on.

00:19:04.311 --> 00:19:07.856
But when I got to Earth,
I found a different kind of prey.

00:19:08.023 --> 00:19:09.775
Explain. Oh!

00:19:09.858 --> 00:19:12.277
You Earthlings
worship celebrity with such fervor

00:19:12.361 --> 00:19:15.781
that I can survive
simply by milking your admiration.

00:19:15.864 --> 00:19:20.536
Milking and milking it
through what we actors call "the process."

00:19:20.619 --> 00:19:23.038
Oh, God,
just kill us already.

00:19:23.205 --> 00:19:27.376
But you all discovered my secret.
And for that, you will pay.

00:19:27.668 --> 00:19:29.086
- Look at me!
- If we do,

00:19:29.169 --> 00:19:31.547
will you stop talking about the process?

00:19:31.713 --> 00:19:33.549
Never. Behold!

00:19:43.267 --> 00:19:46.186
I'll save you, Leela,
Professor and Zoidberg.

00:19:47.729 --> 00:19:48.772
Oops!

00:19:48.981 --> 00:19:51.149
Nonetheless, I finally nailed it.

00:19:51.233 --> 00:19:53.360
Gaze upon this photo of yourself

00:19:53.527 --> 00:19:55.612
and start squirting out some soul-arrhea.

00:19:55.904 --> 00:19:58.365
It doesn't work that way, you imbecile.

00:19:58.448 --> 00:20:01.243
Although it's really
quite a nice portrait.

00:20:01.577 --> 00:20:03.537
The contrast is exquisite.

00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:06.957
And the composition sublime.

00:20:07.249 --> 00:20:09.835
I look spectacular.

00:20:09.918 --> 00:20:13.922
Aw, man. My great photo
only made his ego bigger.

00:20:24.266 --> 00:20:26.435
No. No!

00:20:26.518 --> 00:20:27.561
Oh!

00:20:33.108 --> 00:20:34.943
Hey, Calculon's dead.

00:20:35.110 --> 00:20:37.362
What happened?
Did you save us, Leela?

00:20:37.446 --> 00:20:39.948
Actually, no.
For once, it was Bender.

00:20:40.032 --> 00:20:43.202
Really? Well, thanks
for whatever you did, Bender.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:45.579
It was a lot,
and you'll never be able to pay me back.

00:20:45.746 --> 00:20:47.080
Now, gather round, friends,

00:20:47.164 --> 00:20:49.750
so we can commemorate
this moment in a photo.

00:20:51.668 --> 00:20:52.836
I got to admit,

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:56.006
this time, it'll be a pleasure
to be in your picture.

00:20:56.298 --> 00:20:57.758
Say, "Bender is great."

00:20:57.841 --> 00:20:59.426
Bender is great!

00:21:00.802 --> 00:21:01.845
Neat.